            "key_investigations.4",
            "key_investigations.5",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3"
          ],
          "text": "A septic screen was performed including bloods, blood culture and CRP. Lumbar puncture was deferred given stable respiratory status. CRP rose from 28 to 41 before falling to 18; blood cultures showed no growth at 36 hours and were confirmed negative at 48 hours. IV benzylpenicillin and gentamicin were commenced per neonatal sepsis protocol; on the basis of the clinical picture and initial CRP rise, a decision was made to complete a 5-day course of IV antibiotics, which was done on day 5. Routine newborn checks were completed and the newborn hearing screen was passed.",
